   "he": "הַשּׁוּלְחָן, אׇרְכּוֹ עֲשָׂרָה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna cites the opinion of Rabbi Yehuda: As for «the Table, its length is ten» handbreadths and its width is five handbreadths. Five handbreadths of each loaf of the shewbread, each of which is bent upward, protrude from the Table; two and a half handbreadths on each side. Rabbi Meir holds that the width of the Table is six handbreadths. Therefore, only four handbreadths of each loaf protrude from the Table and two handbreadths are bent upward on each side."
  }
